          ":question/problem": "Find $\\det(C)$ for\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Expand across the top row with signs $+,-,+$. Delete each entry's row and column to form its minor, then subtract the diagonal products. Terms with a zero top-row entry vanish.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{12}&=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=2\\cdot (-3)-4\\cdot 1 \\\\ &=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(C)&=0M_{11}-(-4)M_{12}+0M_{13} \\\\ &=0-(-4)(-10)+0 \\\\ &=0-40+0 \\\\ &=-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
