          ":question/problem": "Find $\\det(C)$ for\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$\\det(C)=${{field-1}}.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Expand across the top row with signs $+,-,+$. Delete each entry's row and column to form its minor, then subtract the diagonal products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{11}&=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-1) \\\\ &=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{12}&=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=2\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 2 \\\\ &=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M_{13}&=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2 \\\\ &=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombine the signed contributions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(C)&=(-3)M_{11}-2M_{12}+(-3)M_{13} \\\\ &=(-3)(5)-2(-2)+(-3)(-4) \\\\ &=-15+4+12 \\\\ &=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
